  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is the structure of the Earth?', 'Crust, mantle, outer core and inner core.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is a tectonic plate?', 'A large section of the Earth''s crust that moves slowly on the mantle.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What causes plates to move?', 'Convection currents in the mantle, and slab pull.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is a destructive plate margin?', 'Where an oceanic plate is forced under a continental plate, causing earthquakes and violent volcanoes.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is a constructive plate margin?', 'Where plates move apart and magma rises to form new crust, causing gentle volcanoes.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is a conservative plate margin?', 'Where plates slide past each other, causing earthquakes but no volcanoes.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is a collision margin?', 'Where two continental plates collide, forming fold mountains.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is the focus of an earthquake?', 'The point underground where the earthquake starts.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is the epicentre?', 'The point on the surface directly above the focus.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'How are earthquakes measured?', 'Using the moment magnitude scale (or Richter scale) and a seismometer.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is a composite volcano?', 'A steep-sided volcano made of layers of ash and lava, with explosive eruptions.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is a shield volcano?', 'A wide, gently sloping volcano made of runny lava, with gentle eruptions.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is a hotspot?', 'An area of volcanic activity away from plate margins, e.g. Hawaii.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What are the primary effects of earthquakes?', 'Buildings collapse, roads and bridges are damaged, and people are killed or injured.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What are the secondary effects of earthquakes?', 'Fires, tsunamis, landslides, disease, and homelessness.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is a tsunami?', 'A large sea wave caused by an earthquake under the ocean.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What are the primary effects of volcanoes?', 'Lava flows, pyroclastic flows, ash falls and gas emissions.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What are the secondary effects of volcanoes?', 'Lahars (mudflows), flooding, loss of tourism, and fertile soils in the long term.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'Why do people live near volcanoes?', 'Fertile soils, tourism, geothermal energy and minerals.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'How can the effects of earthquakes be reduced?', 'Earthquake-proof buildings, education, emergency plans, and early warning systems.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is an earthquake-proof building?', 'A building designed to withstand shaking, e.g. with deep foundations, cross-bracing and shock absorbers.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'How can volcanic eruptions be predicted?', 'Monitoring ground swelling, gas emissions and small earthquakes.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'Why do earthquakes have more impact in poorer countries?', 'Poor-quality buildings, fewer emergency services, and less preparation.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'Give an example of an earthquake in a richer country.', 'Japan (Tōhoku 2011) or Christchurch, New Zealand (2011).', 24),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'Give an example of an earthquake in a poorer country.', 'Nepal (2015) or Haiti (2010).', 25),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is the Pacific Ring of Fire?', 'A zone around the Pacific Ocean with many volcanoes and earthquakes.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is a pyroclastic flow?', 'A fast-moving cloud of hot gas, ash and rock.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is a lahar?', 'A mudflow of volcanic material mixed with water.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is hazard mapping?', 'Mapping areas at risk from hazards to plan land use and evacuation.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is the magnitude of an earthquake?', 'A measure of the energy released by an earthquake.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'What is a natural hazard?', 'A natural process or event that poses a threat to people and property.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'What is hazard risk?', 'The probability or chance that a natural hazard will happen and affect people.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'What causes global atmospheric circulation?', 'Unequal heating of the Earth — the Equator receives more energy than the poles.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'What pressure is found at the Equator?', 'Low pressure, where warm air rises (the ITCZ).', 4),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'What pressure is found at 30° north and south?', 'High pressure, where cool air sinks — this is where hot deserts are found.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'What are trade winds?', 'Surface winds blowing from the sub-tropical high (30°) towards the Equator.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'What are the westerlies?', 'Surface winds blowing from 30° towards 60°, bringing mild, wet Atlantic weather to the UK.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'What are the three circulation cells in each hemisphere?', 'The Hadley cell, the Ferrel cell and the Polar cell.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'Where do tropical storms form?', 'Over warm oceans between about 5° and 30° north and south of the Equator.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'What sea temperature do tropical storms need?', 'At least 26–27°C.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'Why don''t tropical storms form at the Equator?', 'The Coriolis effect is too weak to make the air spin.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'What powers a tropical storm?', 'Latent heat released as water vapour condenses in rising air.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'What is the eye of a tropical storm?', 'The calm, clear centre with sinking air and the lowest pressure.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'What is the eye wall?', 'The ring of tall cloud around the eye, with the strongest winds and heaviest rain.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'Why do tropical storms weaken over land?', 'They lose their supply of warm, moist air and are slowed by friction.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'What is a storm surge?', 'A rise in sea level caused by strong winds and low pressure pushing water onshore.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'How might climate change affect tropical storm intensity?', 'More storms are likely to reach the highest categories, with heavier rain.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'How might climate change affect tropical storm distribution?', 'Storms may form further from the tropics as more ocean reaches 26–27°C.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'When and where did Typhoon Haiyan strike?', 'November 2013, the Philippines — especially Tacloban on Leyte.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'How many people died in Typhoon Haiyan?', 'Over 6,300, with around 1,000 more missing.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'How high was Haiyan''s storm surge?', 'Up to 5–6 metres in Tacloban.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'Give a secondary effect of Typhoon Haiyan.', 'Food and water shortages led to disease and looting; 6 million people lost their income.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'Give an immediate response to Typhoon Haiyan.', '800,000 people evacuated before landfall; international aid from the UK, USA and NGOs.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'Give a long-term response to Typhoon Haiyan.', 'Build Back Better reconstruction, cash-for-work, new cyclone shelters and mangrove replanting.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'What are the four ways of reducing tropical storm effects?', 'Monitoring, prediction, protection and planning.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'Give an example of protection against tropical storms.', 'Raised cyclone shelters in Bangladesh, storm-surge barriers or buildings on stilts.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'What caused the Somerset Levels floods of 2013–14?', 'A series of Atlantic depressions brought the wettest winter on record onto flat, low-lying land.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'Give a long-term response to the Somerset Levels floods.', 'A £100 million Flood Action Plan: 8 km of rivers dredged, pumps upgraded, banks raised.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'What is the UK''s highest recorded temperature?', '40.3°C at Coningsby, Lincolnshire, on 19 July 2022.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Weather Hazards', 'Give evidence that UK weather is becoming more extreme.', 'All ten warmest years since 2002, record rainfall in 2014 and 2015, and more frequent major floods.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'What is climate change?', 'A long-term change in the Earth''s climate, including temperature and rainfall patterns.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'What is the greenhouse effect?', 'Gases in the atmosphere trap heat from the Sun, keeping the Earth warm.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'What is the enhanced greenhouse effect?', 'Human activities increase greenhouse gases, trapping more heat and causing global warming.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'Name three greenhouse gases.', 'Carbon dioxide, methane and nitrous oxide.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'What are the human causes of climate change?', 'Burning fossil fuels, deforestation, farming (methane from cattle), and industry.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'What are the natural causes of climate change?', 'Changes in the Earth''s orbit, volcanic eruptions and variations in solar output.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'What is the evidence for climate change?', 'Rising global temperatures, melting ice caps, rising sea levels, and ice core records.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'What do ice cores show?', 'Air bubbles trapped in ice show past levels of CO₂ and temperature.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'What are the effects of climate change on the environment?', 'Rising sea levels, melting ice, more extreme weather, and loss of habitats.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'What are the effects of climate change on people?', 'Flooding, food shortages, water shortages, and health problems.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'What is mitigation?', 'Reducing the causes of climate change, e.g. cutting emissions.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'What is adaptation?', 'Changing how we live to cope with the effects of climate change.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'Give examples of mitigation.', 'Renewable energy, planting trees, carbon capture, and international agreements.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'Give examples of adaptation.', 'Flood defences, drought-resistant crops, and changing farming practices.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'What is carbon capture and storage?', 'Capturing CO₂ from power stations and storing it underground.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'What is the Paris Agreement?', 'A 2015 international agreement to limit global warming to well below 2 °C.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'What is a carbon footprint?', 'The total amount of greenhouse gases produced by a person, organisation or activity.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'How can individuals reduce their carbon footprint?', 'Using public transport, saving energy, recycling, and eating less meat.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'How does climate change affect the UK?', 'Hotter summers, wetter winters, more flooding and rising sea levels.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'How does climate change affect poorer countries?', 'They are often more vulnerable to droughts, floods and storms, with fewer resources to adapt.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'What is sea-level rise caused by?', 'Melting ice sheets and glaciers, and thermal expansion of water.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'What is thermal expansion?', 'Water expanding as it warms, raising sea levels.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'What is the Quaternary period?', 'The last 2.6 million years, with glacial and interglacial periods.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'What is an interglacial period?', 'A warmer period between glacial periods.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'How does deforestation contribute to climate change?', 'Trees absorb CO₂; removing them increases CO₂ in the atmosphere.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'What is the role of methane in climate change?', 'Methane is a powerful greenhouse gas released by cattle, rice farming and landfill.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'What is renewable energy?', 'Energy from sources that won''t run out, e.g. wind, solar and hydroelectric power.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'What is a climate refugee?', 'Someone forced to move because of the effects of climate change.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'How do rising temperatures affect ecosystems?', 'Species may move, adapt or become extinct, e.g. coral bleaching.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Climate Change', 'What is coral bleaching?', 'Corals expel algae when water is too warm, turning white and possibly dying.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What is an ecosystem?', 'A community of living things interacting with each other and their non-living environment.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What is a biome?', 'A large-scale ecosystem, e.g. tropical rainforest or hot desert.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'Where are tropical rainforests found?', 'Near the equator, e.g. the Amazon, Congo Basin and Southeast Asia.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What is the climate of a tropical rainforest?', 'Hot (about 27 °C) and wet all year, with over 2000 mm of rain.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What are the layers of the rainforest?', 'Emergent layer, canopy, understorey and forest floor.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What is the canopy?', 'The dense layer of tree tops that absorbs most sunlight.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What are buttress roots?', 'Large roots that support tall trees in shallow soils.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What are drip tips?', 'Pointed leaves that allow heavy rain to run off quickly.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What are lianas?', 'Woody vines that climb trees to reach sunlight.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What are epiphytes?', 'Plants that grow on other plants to reach light, e.g. orchids.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'How are animals adapted to the rainforest?', 'E.g. sloths move slowly and are camouflaged; monkeys have prehensile tails; frogs have sticky feet.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What is the nutrient cycle in rainforests?', 'Nutrients are rapidly recycled from leaf litter to plants, so the soil is poor.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'Why is rainforest soil infertile?', 'Heavy rain washes nutrients away (leaching), and nutrients are held in plants.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What is biodiversity?', 'The variety of living things in an area.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'Why do rainforests have high biodiversity?', 'Warm, wet climate all year allows plants to grow quickly, providing many habitats.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What is deforestation?', 'The cutting down or removal of forests.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What are the causes of deforestation?', 'Logging, cattle ranching, farming (e.g. palm oil and soya), mining, road building and hydroelectric dams.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What are the impacts of deforestation?', 'Loss of biodiversity, soil erosion, climate change, and loss of indigenous people''s homes.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'How does deforestation contribute to climate change?', 'Trees store carbon; burning or cutting them releases CO₂, and fewer trees absorb CO₂.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What is sustainable forestry?', 'Managing forests so trees are replanted and the forest can continue to provide resources.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What is selective logging?', 'Only cutting down some mature trees, leaving the rest of the forest intact.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What is ecotourism?', 'Tourism that conserves the environment and benefits local people.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What is agroforestry?', 'Growing crops and trees together, protecting soil and providing resources.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What is debt-for-nature swap?', 'A country''s debt is reduced in exchange for protecting its rainforest.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What role do indigenous people play in rainforests?', 'They often live sustainably and help protect forests from exploitation.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What is a food web?', 'A diagram showing how feeding relationships are linked in an ecosystem.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What is a producer?', 'An organism that makes its own food through photosynthesis, e.g. plants.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What is a consumer?', 'An organism that eats other organisms.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'What is a decomposer?', 'An organism that breaks down dead material, releasing nutrients, e.g. fungi and bacteria.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Ecosystems and Tropical Rainforests', 'Why is the Amazon rainforest important globally?', 'It stores carbon, regulates climate, has huge biodiversity, and provides medicines.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'What is a hot desert?', 'An area with very low rainfall (under 250 mm a year) and high daytime temperatures.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'Where are hot deserts found?', 'Around 30° north and south of the equator, e.g. the Sahara and Thar deserts.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'What is the climate of a hot desert?', 'Very hot days, cold nights and very little rainfall.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'Why are desert nights cold?', 'Clear skies allow heat to escape quickly.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'How are plants adapted to hot deserts?', 'Cacti store water, have spines instead of leaves, and have long or wide roots.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'How are animals adapted to hot deserts?', 'Camels store fat in humps and have wide feet; many animals are nocturnal.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'What is desert soil like?', 'Sandy or stony, dry, and low in nutrients.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'What is desertification?', 'The process by which land becomes desert-like due to climate change and human activity.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'What are the causes of desertification?', 'Overgrazing, overcultivation, deforestation, population growth and climate change.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'Where is desertification a problem?', 'In semi-arid areas such as the Sahel in Africa.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'How can desertification be reduced?', 'Planting trees, water conservation, appropriate technology, and improving farming methods.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'What are magic stones (bunds)?', 'Lines of stones that slow water runoff and trap soil, reducing erosion.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'What opportunities do hot deserts offer?', 'Mining, energy (solar), farming with irrigation, and tourism.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'What challenges do hot deserts present?', 'Extreme temperatures, water shortages, and poor accessibility.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'What is irrigation?', 'Artificially watering crops.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'What is solar energy''s potential in deserts?', 'Deserts receive lots of sunshine, making them ideal for solar power plants.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'What is the Great Green Wall?', 'A project to plant a belt of trees across the Sahel to stop desertification.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'What is an oasis?', 'A fertile area in a desert where water is found.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'What is a nomad?', 'A person who moves from place to place with their animals to find food and water.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'What is overgrazing?', 'When too many animals graze an area, removing vegetation and exposing soil.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'What is overcultivation?', 'When land is farmed too intensively, exhausting the soil.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'Why are desert ecosystems fragile?', 'Low rainfall and extreme conditions mean they recover slowly from damage.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'What is biodiversity like in hot deserts?', 'Lower than rainforests, but many species are specially adapted.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'How does climate change affect hot deserts?', 'Higher temperatures and less rainfall may make them hotter and drier, expanding their area.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'What is a sand dune in a desert?', 'A hill of sand shaped by the wind.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'What is the water cycle like in deserts?', 'Low rainfall and high evaporation mean little water is stored.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'What is the role of tourism in deserts?', 'It provides jobs and income, but can put pressure on water and fragile environments.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'What is mining''s impact in deserts?', 'It provides jobs and resources but uses water and can damage landscapes.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'What is the Thar Desert?', 'A hot desert in north-west India and Pakistan.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Hot Deserts', 'What is the Sahel?', 'A semi-arid region south of the Sahara, at risk of desertification.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'What are the two main types of cold environment?', 'Polar (ice sheets, e.g. Antarctica) and tundra (treeless land fringing the Arctic).', 1),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'Where is tundra found?', 'Roughly 60°–75°N in northern Canada, Alaska, northern Russia and Scandinavia.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'What is permafrost?', 'Ground that stays frozen for at least two consecutive years.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'What is the active layer?', 'The top layer of ground above the permafrost that thaws each summer.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'Why is the tundra waterlogged in summer?', 'Meltwater cannot drain through the impermeable permafrost below.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'How cold do polar winters get?', 'Often below −50°C; Antarctica''s record is −89.2°C.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'How much precipitation do polar areas get?', 'Under 250 mm a year — they are polar deserts.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'Why are polar areas so cold?', 'Low-angle sunlight is spread out and high-albedo snow and ice reflect most of it.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'How long is the tundra growing season?', 'About 6–10 weeks.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'Why can''t trees grow in the tundra?', 'Permafrost stops roots growing deep and the summer is too short and cold.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'Why are tundra soils infertile?', 'They are thin, acidic and decomposition is very slow, so peat builds up.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'How do plants protect permafrost?', 'Vegetation and peat insulate the ground from summer heat.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'Give two plant adaptations to the tundra.', 'Low cushion shapes to avoid wind, and shallow roots in the active layer.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'Give two animal adaptations to cold environments.', 'Thick fur or blubber for insulation, and small extremities to reduce heat loss.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'Why do caribou migrate?', 'To find food and avoid the harshest winter conditions — up to 5,000 km a year.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'Why is biodiversity low in cold environments?', 'The harsh climate allows few species, so food webs are simple.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'Why are cold environment food webs fragile?', 'With few species, losing one (e.g. lemmings) affects many others.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'What is the main economic opportunity in Alaska?', 'Oil, especially from Prudhoe Bay on the North Slope.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'What is the Alaska Permanent Fund?', 'A fund built from oil revenue that pays every resident an annual dividend.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'Give two other opportunities in Alaska.', 'Fishing (about 60% of US seafood) and tourism (over 2 million visitors a year).', 20),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'Give two challenges of developing Alaska.', 'Extreme cold and inaccessibility — vast distances and few roads.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'Why are Alaskan buildings raised on piles?', 'To stop heat from the building thawing the permafrost and causing subsidence.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'How was the Trans-Alaska Pipeline designed?', 'Raised on supports with heat pipes, built in a zigzag, with crossings for caribou.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'What happened in the Exxon Valdez disaster?', 'In 1989, about 41 million litres of oil spilled into Prince William Sound, killing wildlife.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'What is a wilderness area?', 'A natural area largely undisturbed by human activity.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'Why are cold environments valuable?', 'Scientific research (ice cores), unique wildlife, carbon storage and indigenous cultures.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'Why are cold environments fragile?', 'Slow plant growth, slow decomposition and simple food webs mean damage lasts for decades.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'What does the Antarctic Treaty do?', 'Reserves Antarctica for peaceful scientific research; its Madrid Protocol bans mining.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'Give an example of a government protecting a cold environment.', 'The Arctic National Wildlife Refuge (ANWR) in Alaska protects 78,000 km².', 29),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Cold Environments', 'Why is thawing permafrost a climate risk?', 'It releases methane and CO₂, causing more warming — a positive feedback.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What are the four processes of coastal erosion?', 'Hydraulic action, abrasion, attrition and solution.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is hydraulic action?', 'Waves force air into cracks in the cliff, which breaks the rock apart.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is abrasion?', 'Rocks carried by waves are thrown against the cliff, wearing it away.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is attrition?', 'Rocks carried by waves knock against each other, becoming smaller and rounder.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is solution?', 'Seawater dissolves soluble rocks such as chalk and limestone.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is longshore drift?', 'The movement of sediment along the coast by waves approaching at an angle.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is the swash?', 'The movement of water up the beach after a wave breaks.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is the backwash?', 'The movement of water back down the beach under gravity.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a constructive wave?', 'A low, gentle wave with a strong swash and weak backwash, which builds up beaches.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a destructive wave?', 'A tall, steep wave with a weak swash and strong backwash, which erodes beaches.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is fetch?', 'The distance over which the wind blows across open water, affecting wave size.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'How is a headland formed?', 'Resistant rock erodes more slowly than softer rock, leaving land sticking out into the sea.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'How is a bay formed?', 'Softer rock is eroded more quickly, forming a curved inlet between headlands.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'How is a stack formed?', 'Waves erode a crack into a cave, then an arch; the arch roof collapses, leaving a stack.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a stump?', 'The remains of a stack after it has been eroded further.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a wave-cut platform?', 'A flat area of rock at the base of a cliff, left as the cliff retreats through erosion.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'How is a spit formed?', 'Longshore drift carries sediment past a bend in the coastline, where it is deposited in the sea.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a bar?', 'A spit that grows across a bay, joining two headlands and sometimes trapping a lagoon.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a beach?', 'A deposit of sand and shingle along the coast, formed by constructive waves.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a sand dune?', 'A hill of sand formed when wind blows sand inland, trapped by vegetation such as marram grass.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is hard engineering?', 'Building artificial structures to control the sea, e.g. sea walls, groynes and rock armour.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is soft engineering?', 'Working with natural processes to manage the coast, e.g. beach nourishment and dune regeneration.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a sea wall?', 'A concrete wall that reflects waves back out to sea; effective but expensive.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a groyne?', 'A wooden or rock barrier built out to sea to trap sediment moved by longshore drift.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is rock armour?', 'Large boulders placed at the foot of a cliff to absorb wave energy.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is beach nourishment?', 'Adding sand or shingle to a beach to make it wider, absorbing wave energy.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is managed retreat?', 'Allowing the coast to erode or flood naturally in low-value areas.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is sea-level rise''s effect on coasts?', 'It increases flooding and erosion, threatening homes, farmland and habitats.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a Shoreline Management Plan?', 'A plan that decides how each stretch of coast should be managed: hold the line, advance, retreat or do nothing.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Coastal Landscapes in the UK', 'What is mass movement at the coast?', 'The downhill movement of material under gravity, e.g. slumping and rockfalls.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What is the source of a river?', 'Where the river begins, often in upland areas.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What is the mouth of a river?', 'Where the river meets the sea or a lake.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a tributary?', 'A smaller river that joins a larger one.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a confluence?', 'The point where two rivers meet.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a drainage basin?', 'The area of land drained by a river and its tributaries.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a watershed?', 'The boundary of a drainage basin, usually high ground.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'How does a river change from source to mouth?', 'It becomes wider and deeper, with a greater discharge and gentler gradient.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What is vertical erosion?', 'Erosion that deepens the river channel, common in the upper course.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What is lateral erosion?', 'Erosion that widens the river channel, common in the middle and lower course.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What are the four types of river transportation?', 'Traction, saltation, suspension and solution.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What is traction?', 'Large boulders are rolled along the river bed.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What is saltation?', 'Small pebbles bounce along the river bed.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What is suspension?', 'Fine particles are carried in the water.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'When does a river deposit sediment?', 'When it loses energy, e.g. when it slows down on the inside of a bend or enters the sea.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'How is a waterfall formed?', 'Soft rock beneath hard rock is eroded, creating an overhang that collapses; the waterfall retreats, leaving a gorge.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a gorge?', 'A steep-sided valley formed as a waterfall retreats upstream.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a V-shaped valley?', 'A steep valley in the upper course, formed by vertical erosion and weathering.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What is interlocking spurs?', 'Hills that stick out alternately on either side of a river in the upper course.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'How is a meander formed?', 'Erosion on the outside of a bend (fast flow) and deposition on the inside (slow flow).', 19),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'How is an oxbow lake formed?', 'Erosion narrows the neck of a meander until the river cuts through it during a flood; deposition seals off the old loop.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a floodplain?', 'Flat land either side of a river in the lower course, covered with deposits during floods.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a levée?', 'A raised bank along a river, formed by deposition of sediment during floods.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a hydrograph?', 'A graph showing river discharge over time, often in relation to rainfall.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What is lag time?', 'The time between peak rainfall and peak discharge.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What factors increase flood risk?', 'Heavy rainfall, impermeable rock, steep slopes, urbanisation and deforestation.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'How does urbanisation increase flood risk?', 'Impermeable surfaces increase surface runoff, and drains carry water quickly to rivers.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a flood defence?', 'A structure or strategy to reduce flooding, e.g. dams, embankments, flood relief channels.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a flood relief channel?', 'An artificial channel that diverts water away from a town when river levels are high.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What is river restoration?', 'Returning a river to a more natural state to reduce flood risk and improve habitats.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.8', 'River Landscapes in the UK', 'What is flood zoning?', 'Restricting building on floodplains in areas at high risk of flooding.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a glacier?', 'A large mass of ice that moves slowly downhill under gravity.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What is plucking?', 'Ice freezes onto rocks and pulls them away as the glacier moves.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What is abrasion by glaciers?', 'Rocks frozen into the base of the glacier scrape the rock below like sandpaper.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What is freeze–thaw weathering?', 'Water in cracks freezes and expands, widening the crack until the rock breaks.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a corrie?', 'An armchair-shaped hollow on a mountainside, formed by glacial erosion; it may contain a lake (tarn).', 5),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What is an arête?', 'A sharp, knife-edge ridge between two corries.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a pyramidal peak?', 'A sharp mountain peak formed when three or more corries erode back to back.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a U-shaped valley?', 'A wide, flat-bottomed valley with steep sides, formed by a glacier.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a truncated spur?', 'A cut-off end of a spur, eroded by a glacier as it moved down the valley.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a hanging valley?', 'A small valley left high above a main glacial valley, often with a waterfall.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a ribbon lake?', 'A long, narrow lake in the bottom of a U-shaped valley.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What is moraine?', 'Rocks and sediment deposited by a glacier.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a terminal moraine?', 'A ridge of material marking the furthest point reached by a glacier.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What is lateral moraine?', 'Material deposited along the sides of a glacier.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a drumlin?', 'An egg-shaped hill of glacial deposits, with a blunt end facing the direction the ice came from.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What is an erratic?', 'A boulder carried by a glacier and deposited in an area with different rock.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What is till?', 'Unsorted sediment deposited by a glacier.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'Where are glaciated landscapes found in the UK?', 'In upland areas such as the Lake District, Snowdonia and the Scottish Highlands.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What was the last glacial period?', 'The most recent ice age, which ended about 10,000 years ago.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'How is glaciated land used?', 'Farming (sheep), tourism, forestry, quarrying, and hydroelectric power.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What are the impacts of tourism in glaciated areas?', 'Jobs and income, but also footpath erosion, traffic congestion and litter.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What is footpath erosion?', 'Damage to paths from many walkers, removing vegetation and exposing soil.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'How can footpath erosion be managed?', 'Laying stone paths, fencing off areas, and signs to keep walkers on paths.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a honeypot site?', 'A popular tourist location that attracts large numbers of visitors.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What conflicts can occur in glaciated areas?', 'Between farmers, tourists, conservationists and residents over land use.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a national park?', 'A protected area of countryside managed for conservation and recreation.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'Why are glaciers retreating?', 'Global warming is melting ice faster than it accumulates.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a glacial trough?', 'Another name for a U-shaped valley.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What is a tarn?', 'A small lake in a corrie.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '1.9', 'Glacial Landscapes in the UK', 'What is the difference between erosion and weathering?', 'Weathering breaks down rock in place; erosion wears it away and moves it.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Issues in LICs and NEEs', 'What is urbanisation?', 'The increase in the proportion of people living in towns and cities.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Issues in LICs and NEEs', 'What is a megacity?', 'A city with a population of more than 10 million.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Issues in LICs and NEEs', 'What causes urbanisation?', 'Rural–urban migration and natural increase.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Issues in LICs and NEEs', 'What are push factors?', 'Reasons that make people leave rural areas, e.g. lack of jobs, poor services and natural disasters.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Issues in LICs and NEEs', 'What are pull factors?', 'Reasons that attract people to cities, e.g. jobs, better healthcare and education.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Issues in LICs and NEEs', 'What is natural increase?', 'When the birth rate is higher than the death rate.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Issues in LICs and NEEs', 'Where is urbanisation happening fastest?', 'In lower-income and newly emerging countries in Africa and Asia.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Issues in LICs and NEEs', 'What is a squatter settlement?', 'An area of poor-quality housing built illegally on land the residents don''t own.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Issues in LICs and NEEs', 'What are the problems of squatter settlements?', 'Poor sanitation, lack of clean water, disease, crime, and flood or fire risk.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Issues in LICs and NEEs', 'What is the informal economy?', 'Jobs that aren''t officially recorded or taxed, e.g. street selling.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Issues in LICs and NEEs', 'What is a site-and-service scheme?', 'Authorities provide land with basic services, and residents build their own homes.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Issues in LICs and NEEs', 'What is self-help housing?', 'Residents are given materials and support to improve their own homes.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Issues in LICs and NEEs', 'What is suburbanisation?', 'The movement of people from the inner city to the suburbs.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Issues in LICs and NEEs', 'What is counter-urbanisation?', 'The movement of people from cities to rural areas.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Issues in LICs and NEEs', 'What is re-urbanisation?', 'The movement of people back into city centres, often after regeneration.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Issues in LICs and NEEs', 'What is a global city?', 'A city with major international influence in finance, culture and politics, e.g. London or New York.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Issues in LICs and NEEs', 'What are the challenges of rapid urbanisation?', 'Housing shortages, traffic, pollution, unemployment and pressure on services.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Issues in LICs and NEEs', 'What is urban sprawl?', 'The spread of cities into the surrounding countryside.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Issues in LICs and NEEs', 'What is a brownfield site?', 'Previously developed land that can be reused.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Issues in LICs and NEEs', 'What is a greenfield site?', 'Land that hasn''t been built on before.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Issues in LICs and NEEs', 'What is a sustainable city?', 'A city that meets people''s needs without damaging the environment for future generations.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Issues in LICs and NEEs', 'Give an example of a sustainable urban feature.', 'Public transport, green spaces, recycling schemes and energy-efficient buildings.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'AQA', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Issues in LICs and NEEs', 'What is the CBD?', 'The central business district, the commercial centre of a city.', 23),
